    "turn_idx": 81,
    "turn_text": "I don't know if you knew growing up or anyone from the Gillenwater family, but the Gillenwaters took me down to Ahoe and then to Lukeville. And they rode up because what they were seeing were all these immigrants that were very, very, very, very darkly complex. It turns out they were all from West Africa, they were talking to a man, they asked, does anyone here speak English? Talking to a man, his name was Fahim. He said, I speak English. He said, well, what is this about? And he said, we were invited here by your president and we all know this. We all know to say the word asylum and we were invited here.",
